=====================================================================
PROJECT: "ENDLESS SPRING" STORY MODE (new, fully isolated game mode)
=====================================================================

GOAL
Add a new single-player story game mode based on the novel "Endless
Spring: Part One - Mind Opens" by Ananda Jana. It contains FIVE separate
games. Each game covers a block of story chapters, is playable on its own
(no unlock order, no progress locks), and lasts about 15 minutes. The
games use story-themed boards, story-character pieces and story-specific
rules. They are NOT standard chess.

THE MOST IMPORTANT RULE: TOTAL ISOLATION
Existing game logic must never be affected. Follow all of these:

1. Create ONE new folder: src/endlessSpring/. Every file for this mode
   lives there (plus tests, see below).
2. Every new file name AND every exported identifier uses the prefix Es
   (components, functions, types) or ES_ (constants). Before creating any
   file, search the whole project (find / grep -ril) to confirm the name
   does not already exist. No name may match any file or export anywhere
   else in the project.
3. localStorage keys all start with "endless_spring_". No other keys.
4. Do NOT import from, or modify, any existing game code: engine.ts,
   bot.ts, cullingEngine.ts, cullingBot.ts, craftables.ts, roseRules.ts,
   socket or auth contexts, training files, or any existing component
   except as stated in rule 5. Do NOT use sockets, fetch/network calls, the
   database, ratings, or user stats. Allowed imports: React, lucide-react,
   and files inside src/endlessSpring/.
5. The ONLY edit outside src/endlessSpring/ is in Dashboard.tsx:
   - one lazy import: const EsRoot = React.lazy(() => import(...));
   - one useState(boolean) to open and close the mode;
   - the entry card (see ENTRY BUTTON);
   - rendering <EsRoot onExit={...} /> inside <Suspense> as a full-screen
     overlay (fixed inset-0, high z-index) ONLY when open.
   Do not touch App.tsx, routing, global CSS, the Tailwind config, or any
   other card. The overlay approach means the mode needs no router change.
6. Do not edit src/components/ChessPiece.tsx or any ChessPiece*.tsx file.
   The piece renderer is COPIED (see PIECES AND ART).
7. Copy anything reusable (for example the modal focus-trap hook) into
   src/endlessSpring/ under an Es-prefixed name. Never import the original.
8. No new npm dependencies. Tailwind utility classes only. Any keyframes go
   in a <style> tag inside an Es component, with class and keyframe names
   starting "es-". Respect prefers-reduced-motion.
9. Final report: list of new files, the exact lines changed in
   Dashboard.tsx, and proof that no other file changed (git diff --stat).

