SCREENS AND FLOW (EsRoot)
1. Select screen: 5 cards. Each shows the game number, title, arc name,
   "Chapters X-Y", "about 15 min", a spoiler line ("Contains events from
   chapters X-Y"), a Read on Scribble Hub link (target="_blank"
   rel="noopener noreferrer", using ES_SCRIBBLE_HUB_URL), and a Play button.
   If a save exists for that game, show Continue and Start Over buttons
   instead of Play. Nothing is locked. Exit button top-left. This screen may
   scroll.
2. Story modal (new games only): dark glass, centered, with the title, arc
   name, chapter range and the story script (see STORY TEXTS) and a Begin
   button. Glass recipe: backdrop bg-black/70; panel bg-zinc-950/95
   supports-[backdrop-filter]:bg-zinc-950/65
   supports-[backdrop-filter]:backdrop-blur-xl border border-white/10.
   Escape or X goes back to the select screen. Focus trapped and restored.
3. Game screen. The page must not scroll during play. Layout is
   top bar (title, round counter, Rules button, Exit), HUD line (objective
   plus "next event in N rounds"), board fitted to the free space with a
   ResizeObserver (width and height), and a bottom bar with Undo-free
   controls: Rules, Restart game, and phase-specific action buttons
   (Imagine, Lift, and so on). Controls are at least 44px tall. Must work at
   320x568, 360x640, 390x844, 430x932 and on desktop.
4. End modal: outcome title, 2-3 lines of ending text, the Scribble Hub
   link, Replay and Back to Select buttons.
Exit asks for confirmation if the game is in progress. The game state is
saved after every half-move, so closing the tab never loses a game.

SAVE RULES (EsSaveStore)
Key: endless_spring_save_v1_g1 ... g5. Value: JSON containing version 1,
the full game state (board, pieces, round, phase, flags, cooldowns, seed)
and a timestamp. If the version is unknown or the JSON is invalid, ignore
the save silently. Saving never throws. After load, if it is the opponent's
turn, run the bot.

=====================================================================
COMMON RULES ENGINE (apply to ALL five games)
=====================================================================
COORDINATES. Each board is a grid. x = column, 0 at the left. y = row, 0
at the BOTTOM. Boards in EsGameData are written as arrays of strings with
the TOP row first. '.' = playable, '#' = void. Side A is the player and
starts at the bottom. Side B is the opponent. Neutral pieces belong to
neither side.

TURNS. A "round" = A's turn followed by B's turn. A always moves first. In
a turn the player moves exactly ONE piece, or uses one special action when
that game allows it. No passing. If a side has no legal move its turn is
skipped. (Game 4 gives B a double move, see there.)

MOVING AND CAPTURING. A piece moves to a legal target square. If an enemy
piece stands there, it is captured and removed. You can never land on a
friendly piece, a void square, or a neutral token. Sliding pieces stop at
the first piece or void on the path (a capture is allowed on an enemy
blocker; the ray cannot continue). Jumping pieces ignore pieces and voids
in between but the landing square must be playable. Pieces marked "no
capture" simply cannot move onto enemy-occupied squares.

END-OF-ROUND EVENTS. After B's turn, apply that game's events for the
round number, in the order listed in the game data. Then check the
objectives. The same order always applies, so results are predictable.

OBJECTIVE CHECK ORDER. After every move: (1) A's win condition, (2) A's
loss condition, (3) round limit. If A's win and loss happen at the same
moment, A loses.

NO CHECK RULE. There is no check or checkmate in this mode. Royal pieces
are lost only when captured.

INFORMATION. Everything is visible to the player, except Game 5's hidden
loyalties. Every scheduled event is shown in the HUD in advance ("Water
rises in 2 rounds"). Nothing is random during play. Randomness exists only
in Game 5's start (a stored seed).

THE OPPONENT AI (EsBotBrain)
- Deterministic alpha-beta search, depth 2, 300ms budget, fallback to depth
  1. Same position gives the same move every time.
- Evaluation: material (values in EsGameData) plus game-specific terms
  listed under each game. Tie-break: lowest piece id, then lowest target y,
  then lowest target x.
- Scripted pieces (Crowd flow, Scarecrow flee, Watcher, Torchbearer,
  Yjkstra timing) are moved by EsEvents, not by the search.
- The AI is meant to be beatable. All strengths are constants in
  EsGameData.

PIECE MOVEMENT TABLE (exact, same everywhere)
Directions: O4 = the 4 orthogonal directions, D4 = the 4 diagonals,
8 = all 8.
- dreamer (AJ): 1 step in 8. Captures. 
- keeper (Sunanda): 1 step in 8. Captures. (Opponent version of dreamer.)
- guide (AJX): slides up to 3 squares in O4, OR 1 step in D4. Captures.
- footman: 1 step in O4. Captures.
- shade: knight jump (offsets +-1,+-2 and +-2,+-1). Captures.
- wind: slides up to 3 squares in D4. Captures.
- beam: slides up to 4 squares in O4. Captures.
- scarecrow: 1 step in O4. NO capture. (Royal piece in Game 1.)
- echo: 1 step in O4. No capture. Cannot be captured (see Game 2).
- angel: slides up to 3 in D4. Captures. Has one special (Game 2).
- investigator: slides up to 2 in O4. NO capture. Special (Game 2).
- observer: 1 step in O4. Captures.
- boat: 1 step in O4. NO capture. Fragile, see Game 3.
- guest: 1 step in O4. Captures.
- undertow: 1 step in 8. Captures.
- rescuer: slides up to 4 in O4. Captures. Special Lift (Game 3).
- banded: 1 step in 8. Captures.
- crowd (token): neutral, never captured by A, moved by flow (Game 4).
- torchbearer: 1 step in O4. Cannot be captured. Special (Game 4).
- kin: neutral hidden piece (Game 5).
- watcher: 1 step in O4. Captures. Cannot be captured.
- yjkstra: slides up to 2 in 8. Captures. Acts on odd rounds only.
Piece values (for evaluation and tie-breaks): footman 1, shade 3, wind 3,
beam 4, guide 4, keeper 2, dreamer 2, observer 1, banded 1, guest 1,
undertow 2, rescuer 4, angel 3, others 0.

=====================================================================
GAME 1 - LIGHT AND SHADOW KINGDOM (Chapters 1-6, arc: Commemoration-Fractures)
=====================================================================
Board: 8 columns x 8 rows, all playable. Round limit 30.
Sides: A = Shadow Kingdom (AJ). B = Light Kingdom (Sunanda).
Pieces per side (8). Side A (y=0 and y=1): shade (1,0), wind (2,0),
scarecrow (3,0), dreamer (4,0), beam (5,0), footmen (2,1), (3,1), (4,1).
Side B is the 180-degree mirror (x -> 7-x, y -> 7-y), using keeper instead
of dreamer.

SHADOW LINE. A variable S starts at 4. Columns x < S are SHADOW, columns
x >= S are LIGHT. At the end of round 4, S becomes 3. At the end of round
8, S becomes 2. S never changes again. This represents noon shrinking the
shadow.

HIDDEN RULE. A piece standing on a shadow square can be captured only by a
capturing piece whose origin square is within 1 square (Chebyshev
distance 1) of the target. Shade, wind and beam cannot capture a hidden
piece from afar. This applies equally to both sides. Show the shadow as a
dark translucent band over columns x < S; animate S changes (200ms).

PHASES AND EVENTS.
- Phase 1, rounds 1-10 "Morning": only the shadow line rule.
- Round 5 end: the Shrine of Ryoshin appears on the first EMPTY square from
  this list: (3,3), (4,4), (3,4), (4,3). A piece that ENDS its move on the
  shrine removes it and gives its owner a Blessing: at the start of that
  side's next turn they make two moves in a row with two DIFFERENT pieces.
  Only one Blessing exists per game.
- Phase 2, rounds 11-20 "Storm": beam and wind slide at most 2 squares
  (instead of 4 and 3). Show a grey storm tint.
- Phase 3, rounds 21-30 "The Fire": at the end of round 20+k (k = 0..9) the
  square FIRE[k] gets "smoke"; at the end of the next round it becomes
  "fire". FIRE = [(3,3),(4,4),(3,4),(4,3),(2,3),(5,4),(2,4),(5,3),(3,2),(4,5)].
  Smoke squares are still enterable. Fire squares are void for all pieces,
  and any piece standing on a square when it turns to fire is destroyed.

WIN: capture the enemy scarecrow, or an enemy scarecrow is destroyed by fire.
LOSS: your scarecrow is captured or burned.
AT THE ROUND LIMIT (end of round 30, after events): compare the total piece
values of the surviving pieces. Higher wins. Equal is a "Dusk Draw"
ending (counts as story complete).
AI evaluation extras: +3 for each own piece on a shadow square, -8 if the
own scarecrow is on a light square with an enemy beam or wind in line,
+20 for adjacency to the Shrine when it exists.

=====================================================================
GAME 2 - THE INVESTIGATOR (Chapters 7-12, arc: Commemoration-Fractures)
=====================================================================
Board: 9 columns x 5 rows (top row first):
  y4: #...#...#
  y3: ##.###.##
  y2: .........
  y1: ##.###.##
  y0: #...#...#
Round limit 30. Tiles: NOTEBOOK (2,0), SLIP (6,4), EXIT (8,2).
Side A: dreamer AJ (4,2), footmen (3,2) and (5,2).
Side B: investigator (7,2), observers (6,0) and (2,4).

ITEMS. When AJ ENDS a move on the Notebook or Slip tile, that item is
collected and the tile becomes normal. The EXIT tile is a normal tile
until AJ holds BOTH items: then AJ ending its move on EXIT wins. Other
pieces cannot collect items.

QUESTIONING. At the end of every B turn: (a) every echo within 1 square of
the investigator is destroyed; (b) if the investigator is within 1 square
of AJ, AJ gets one Question (maximum one per round). THREE Questions = LOSS.

IMAGINE (A's special action, use INSTEAD of moving). Place one echo on any
empty playable non-tile square within 2 squares of AJ. Cooldown: 3 rounds
between uses (first use is available in round 1). Maximum 3 echoes at once.
Echoes cannot be captured. An echo that survives to the END of the phase
in which it was made becomes a REAL footman (it can then capture and be
captured). In Phase 3, an echo becomes real at the end of the round it was
placed. Echoes block movement for all pieces.

THE ANGEL. At the start of round 11 an angel (side A) appears on (4,2), or
the first empty square among (3,2), (5,2), (4,1)... use the order (4,2),
(3,2), (5,2), (2,2), (6,2). Intercept (once per game): when B captures any
A piece within 3 squares of the angel (including the angel), the player
may CANCEL that capture; the capturing piece goes back to its origin and
B's turn ends. Show a confirm button "Intercept?" before the capture is
final.

PHASES: 1 = rounds 1-10 "The Classroom"; 2 = rounds 11-20 "The Clearing"
(angel exists); 3 = rounds 21-30 "A World of My Own" (echoes real at once).
WIN: AJ ends a move on EXIT holding both items.
LOSS: AJ captured, 3 Questions, or round limit reached.
AI evaluation extras: the investigator moves toward AJ; observers move
toward items' rooms and toward AJ; -50 if AJ holds both items.

=====================================================================
GAME 3 - NO WAY BACK (Chapters 13-17, arc: The Anomalies Arc)
=====================================================================
Three stages on three different boards. At each stage change, the rosters
are RESET to the stage's fixed roster (only the boat's survival matters,
nothing else carries over). Round limit per stage: 10, 9, 8. Saved state
includes the stage number.
The BOAT (paper boat, a piece) is the thing to protect in all stages. LOSS
in any stage: the boat is captured, sinks, or the stage round limit is
reached. WIN: the boat reaches the stage's PASSAGE (2 adjacent squares); in
stage 3 that wins the game.

STAGE 1 "The Beachside Hotel": 5x5 board, all playable, WRAP-AROUND (a
torus): a move that leaves one edge continues from the opposite edge.
Sliders wrap but cannot pass through their own starting square. Knights
wrap. Side A: boat (2,0), shade (1,0), wind (3,0). Side B: guests at (0,2)
and (4,2). PASSAGE squares: (2,2) and (3,2). The passage can be entered only
when "loops" >= 2. Each time the boat itself crosses an edge by wrapping,
loops +1 (shown in the HUD "Loops 1/2"). 

STAGE 2 "The Ruins": 7x7 board (top row first):
  y6: .......
  y5: .#...#.
  y4: .......
  y3: ..#.#..
  y2: .......
  y1: .#...#.
  y0: .......
Side A: boat (3,0), rescuer (2,0), wind (4,0). Side B: undertows at (1,4)
and (5,4). PASSAGE: (3,6) and (4,6).
Water: at the end of round r (r = 3..9) row y = r-3 floods. A flooded
square limits any piece standing on it to moves of distance 1 (Chebyshev),
for every piece. If the boat is on a flooded row at the end of a round
(after water rises), it SINKS (loss).
LIFT (rescuer's special action, instead of moving): swap places with the
boat if they share a row or column, the distance is at most 3 squares and
the squares between are empty. Cooldown 3 rounds.

STAGE 3 "The Gate of the Fair": 8x6 board (top row first):
  y5: ........
  y4: ..#..#..
  y3: ........
  y2: .#....#.
  y1: ........
  y0: ........
Side A: boat (3,0), dreamer AJ (4,0), shade (2,0). Side B: guests at (1,3)
and (6,3). At the END of round 1, every EMPTY square in row y=0 becomes
void (the gate vanishes behind you); occupied row-0 squares become void as
soon as they are vacated. At the end of rounds 3 and 6 a new guest appears
on (0,5) then (7,5) (or the nearest empty square by ascending y then x).
PASSAGE (winning squares): (3,5) and (4,5).
AI evaluation extras: +10 for each step a guest gets closer (Chebyshev) to
the boat; heavy bonus for threatening the boat.

=====================================================================
GAME 4 - THE FAIR AND THE HOTEL (Chapters 18-24, arc: The Anomalies Arc)
=====================================================================
Three acts. Rosters reset at each act. Save state includes the act.
DOUBLE MOVE: in Act 1 only, B moves up to TWO different banded pieces per
turn (one step each). Show this in the HUD ("The signal is answered: they
move twice").

ACT 1 "Death Procession" (rounds 1-14). Board 9x9 with a stage block of
void squares at x=3..5, y=7..8. Side A: dreamer AJ (4,6), guide AJX (3,6).
Side B: banded at (1,8), (7,8), (0,6), (8,6).
CROWD: 12 neutral tokens start at (1,5),(3,5),(5,5),(7,5),(0,4),(2,4),
(6,4),(8,4),(1,3),(4,3),(7,3),(3,2). Tokens block movement for everyone and
are never captured by A. At the end of every round each token moves 1 step
along its row's flow: rows with even y flow EAST, rows with odd y flow
WEST. If the target is off the board, it wraps to the other edge of that
row. If the target square is void, occupied by a piece or token, the token
stays. Process east-flowing tokens from highest x to lowest, west-flowing
from lowest x to highest.
SHIELD: B's banded may capture a token ONLY if no A piece is within 1
square (Chebyshev) of that token. A captured token is a casualty.
PART THE CROWD (guide AJX's special action, instead of moving): swap places
with an adjacent token (8 directions).
REINFORCEMENTS: at the end of rounds 4, 8 and 12, two new banded appear on
(0,8) and (8,8) (or the nearest empty square by ascending distance, then
ascending y, then x).
WIN (Act 1): AJ ends a move on any square of row y=0. LOSS: AJ captured, or
round 14 ends without escape.
Ending text variant by tokens alive at the end: 8 or more "Mercy", 4-7
"The Cost", 3 or fewer "Silence". It changes the text only.

ACT 2 "Homedoing" (rounds 1-12; a calm, enemy-free puzzle). Board 7x7 (top
row first):
  y6: .......
  y5: .#...#.
  y4: .......
  y3: ...#...
  y2: .......
  y1: .#...#.
  y0: .......
Side A: dreamer AJ (3,0), guide AJX (0,0). Neutral scarecrow (3,6): at the
end of every round, it moves 1 step in O4 to an empty playable neighbour
that MAXIMISES its Chebyshev distance to AJ (tie: maximise Manhattan
distance; tie: lowest y, then lowest x). If none exists it stays. WIN: AJ or
AJX moves onto the scarecrow's square ("found"). LOSS: round 12 ends.

ACT 3 "Burning Conscience" (rounds 1-8). Board 5 columns x 7 rows (top row
first):
  y6: ..R..
  y5: .....
  y4: .....
  y3: .#.#.
  y2: .....
  y1: .....
  y0: .....
R is the RED DOOR at (2,6) (a normal playable square). Side A: dreamer AJ
(2,0), guide AJX (1,0). Neutral torchbearer at (2,5), cannot be captured.
At the end of every round, the torchbearer moves 1 step in O4 along the
shortest path (ties: lowest y, then lowest x) toward AJ, and does not
move onto a piece. STILLNESS: if after its move the torchbearer is next to
an A piece in O4, that piece cannot be moved on A's next turn. WIN: AJ ends
a move on the Red Door. LOSS: round 8 ends. 
Game 4 total rounds up to 34.

=====================================================================
GAME 5 - STATE ONE (Chapters 25-29, arc: State One Arc)
=====================================================================
Three phases. Allies revealed in phase 1 (max 3) carry into phases 2 and 3.
AJ must survive all phases; AJ captured = LOSS.

PHASE 1 "Total Mistrust" (rounds 1-10). Board 7x7, all playable except
(3,3) void. AJ at (3,0). Six KIN pieces (neutral) at (1,2),(5,2),(0,4),
(6,4),(2,5),(4,5). At game start, a seeded shuffle (mulberry32, seed saved
in the save) decides which 3 are ALLIES and which 3 are ENEMIES. The
player does not see this. REVEAL: when any piece ends a move next to a kin
in O4, the kin is revealed. An ally becomes an A footman. An enemy becomes
a B banded and cannot act in the round it was revealed. B has no other
pieces; if B has no banded, its turn is skipped. Phase ends at the end of
round 10, or one round after all six are revealed. Any kin never revealed
vanishes.

PHASE 2 "Archive Library" (rounds 1-14). Board 9x7 (top row first):
  y6: .........
  y5: .##.#.##.
  y4: .........
  y3: .#.###.#.
  y2: .........
  y1: .##.#.##.
  y0: .........
AJ at (0,0); carried allies (up to 3) start at (0,1),(1,0),(0,2) (skipping
any occupied or void square, first empty by listed order). PAPERS on (2,6),
(6,6), (4,4), (2,2), (6,2). The STAIR is (8,6). Watcher starts on (8,6),
moves 1 step in O4 every SECOND round (at the end of rounds 2,4,6,...)
along the shortest path (BFS, ties: lowest y, then lowest x) to AJ, may not
enter a square occupied by another piece EXCEPT it captures A pieces by
moving onto them. It cannot be captured. WIN: AJ holds all 5 papers (a paper
is collected when AJ ends a move on it) and ends a move on the Stair.
LOSS: AJ captured or round 14 ends.

PHASE 3 "Reckoning" (rounds 1-8). Board 5x5, all playable. AJ (2,0); carried
allies on (1,0),(3,0),(2,1) in that order. Yjkstra (B) at (2,4). Yjkstra
moves only on ODD rounds (1,3,5,7) and passes on even rounds ("his
stillness"); his move is chosen by the AI, slide 1-2 in 8 directions,
captures. AJ and allies may capture Yjkstra (alternate ending
"Defiance"). WIN: AJ alive at the end of round 8. In that case play the
end sequence: a third door appears and the screen reads "END OF PART ONE"
with the Scribble Hub link. LOSS: AJ captured ("The held breath breaks").

